# No tests for configuration values

A test that restates a hand-maintained constant, name, table row, or default
is a constant pin. It fails only when someone edits the constant. Delete it.

Test the mechanism that reads the constant with one representative input
instead.

A relation across table rows stays. A key present in two tables, a parent that
exists, or a total that matches can fail for a defect, so that test earns its
place.
